, credits, technical support or programme access.</p></article>
      <article class="partner-card"><h4>2 · Intellectual property</h4><p>TIKVARON retains its brand, product vision, independently developed code, product architecture, business methods, customer relationships and pre-existing IP. Partner background IP remains theirs under a limited, documented licence where needed.</p></article>
      <article class="partner-card"><h4>3 · Customer & data protection</h4><p>Customer ownership, permitted data use, confidentiality, security, retention, deletion, subprocessors and breach notification must be explicit. No partner may reuse customer or farmer data for unrelated purposes.</p></article>
      <article class="partner-card"><h4>4 · Commercial independence</h4><p>No exclusivity, non-compete, right of first refusal, revenue share, minimum spend, hidden fee or lock-in unless separately justified, negotiated and expressly approved by the founder after review.</p></article>
      <article class="partner-card"><h4>5 · Joint development</h4><p>Before work begins, document background IP, new IP ownership, licences, source-code access, open-source obligations, maintenance, derivative works and exit rights. No implied assignment or joint ownership.</p></article>
      <article class="partner-card"><h4>6 · Human accountability</h4><p>Partners may contribute expertise and services, but TIKVARON retains product quality, safety, customer commitments and final business decisions. High-risk agricultural advice requires qualified human governance.</p></article>
    </div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Partnership evaluation criteria</h4><p>Score each dimension from 0 (no evidence) to 5 (strong verified evidence). Do not treat a high score as approval to sign.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Dimension</th><th>What must be demonstrated</th><th>Evidence to retain</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Strategic fit</td><td>Directly advances an approved TIKVARON priority and defined outcome.</td><td>Written scope, target outcome and owner.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Capability/value</td><td>Concrete expertise, technology, funding, farmer access or commercial value unavailable as cheaply elsewhere.</td><td>Offer, deliverables, named resources and value estimate.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Commercial viability</td><td>All fees, credits, co-funding, taxes, payment terms and future costs are understood.</td><td>Written pricing and cost assumptions.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Ownership/IP</td><td>No unacceptable equity, IP assignment, licence, derivative-work or control terms.</td><td>IP schedule and contract clauses reviewed.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Customer/data safety</td><td>Data access is necessary, limited, secure and lawful; customer and farmer interests are protected.</td><td>Data map, security terms, privacy roles and retention plan.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Execution credibility</td><td>Partner has relevant track record, capacity, references and accountable contacts.</td><td>Due diligence notes and references.</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Exit & dependency</td><td>TIKVARON can leave, migrate and continue operating without disproportionate penalty.</td><td>Termination, portability, transition and continuity terms.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div><p><strong>Decision guidance:</strong> 28–35 = strong candidate for formal review; 20–27 = conditional / negotiate; below 20 = defer or reject. Any red-line ownership or control issue overrides the score.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Ownership and intellectual-property safeguards</h4><ul>
      <li>Identify each party's pre-existing IP in a schedule before work starts.</li><li>Do not assign TIKVARON's existing or independently developed IP to a partner.</li><li>Any licence to TIKVARON IP must be purpose-limited, non-exclusive by default, time-bounded where appropriate, and terminable on defined grounds.</li><li>Newly developed IP must be expressly allocated in writing before the work begins; prefer TIKVARON ownership of commissioned core product work, subject to negotiated fair terms and legal review.</li><li>Third-party models, APIs, datasets and open-source components remain subject to their own licences; verify commercial use, data handling and redistribution rights.</li><li>No partner may register TIKVARON marks, domains, accounts or customer relationships in its own name.</li><li>Confidential information is shared only on a need-to-know basis under suitable confidentiality and data-protection terms.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Agreement review checklist — mandatory before signature</h4><ol>
      <li>Confirm legal identity, authority to sign, beneficial ownership and control, sanctions/reputation, payment route and references; repeat screening when risk or ownership changes.</li><li>Define purpose, scope, deliverables, acceptance criteria, milestones, named owners and service levels.</li><li>List all fees, taxes, expenses, credits, renewal charges, minimum commitments and payment triggers.</li><li>Review equity, options, warrants, governance rights, IP assignment, licences, exclusivity, non-compete, revenue share and joint-venture clauses.</li><li>Set confidentiality, privacy roles, data minimisation, security controls, breach notice, subprocessors, retention and deletion.</li><li>Allocate liability, warranties, indemnities, insurance where relevant, dispute resolution and governing law.</li><li>Set term, renewal, termination for convenience/cause, cure periods, transition assistance, data export and continued service arrangements.</li><li>Confirm no public announcement, logo use, case study, customer contact or press release without written permission.</li><li>Obtain independent legal review for material agreements and record the reviewer's comments and resolution.</li><li>Obtain explicit founder approval of the final version and store the signed copy and approval evidence.</li>
    </ol></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Partner risk assessment</h4><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Risk area</th><th>Warning signs</th><th>Required control</th></tr></thead><tbody>
      <tr><td>Ownership/control</td><td>Equity demand, broad IP assignment, veto rights or implied joint ownership.</td><td>Stop negotiation; founder decision and specialist legal review required.</td></tr><tr><td>Lock-in</td><td>Exclusivity, long auto-renewal, proprietary formats or high exit fees.</td><td>Negotiate non-exclusive terms, portability and reasonable exit.</td></tr><tr><td>Financial</td><td>Unclear credits, hidden usage costs, upfront fees or uncapped liability.</td><td>Written total-cost model, spending cap and founder approval.</td></tr><tr><td>Data/security</td><td>Unrestricted farmer/customer data access, unclear subprocessors or reuse.</td><td>Data minimisation, security diligence, access controls and written processing terms.</td></tr><tr><td>Delivery</td><td>Unverified claims, no named team, weak references or vague deliverables.</td><td>Reference checks, milestones, acceptance tests and termination rights.</td></tr><tr><td>Reputation/regulatory</td><td>Misleading claims, conflicts, unsafe advice or unclear regulatory responsibilities.</td><td>Due diligence, approved messaging, human oversight and compliance review.</td></tr>
    </tbody></table></div><p>Classify each risk Low / Medium / High / Critical. Any Critical risk blocks approval until resolved; unresolved ownership, data misuse or unlawful activity is grounds to reject. For Russia-linked counterparties, apply enhanced entity/beneficial-owner/control, transaction, banking and export-control screening before outreach or commitment.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Data protection and cross-border partner controls</h4><p>Before any partner receives personal, farmer, customer, employee or other confidential data, TIKVARON must identify the controller/processor roles, purpose, lawful basis, minimum necessary data, access controls, retention period, deletion/return process, subprocessors, breach notification and audit rights. Any transfer outside Kenya requires a documented assessment of the applicable Data Protection Act requirements and appropriate safeguards; sensitive personal data requires additional safeguards and consent where legally required. Use a written data-processing or data-sharing agreement where applicable. Do not send identifiable customer or farmer data during exploratory partnership discussions.</p><p>Official reference: <a href="https://odpc.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/ODPC-%E2%80%93-Guidance-Notes-for-Cross-border-Data-Transfers.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ODPC Guidance Notes for Cross-border Data Transfers</a> and <a href="https://odpc.go.ke/wp-content/uploads/2026/07/ODPC-%E2%80%93-Guidance-Note-for-Data-Protection-Policies.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">ODPC Guidance Notes for Data Protection Policies</a>. This policy is an operational control, not a legal opinion; obtain Kenyan counsel for the actual transfer and contract.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Mandatory partnership approval gates</h4><ol><li><strong>Gate 0 — Research:</strong> public-source research only; no commitments, confidential disclosure or spend.</li><li><strong>Gate 1 — Discovery:</strong> founder-approved outreach; non-binding discussion only; record recipient, date and evidence.</li><li><strong>Gate 2 — Proposal / pilot:</strong> written scope, budget owner, funding route, deliverables, success measures, costs, safety controls and exit plan.</li><li><strong>Gate 3 — Agreement:</strong> qualified legal review of the exact final version; founder explicitly approves the counterparty, scope, price, duration and document version.</li><li><strong>Gate 4 — Execution:</strong> signed agreement stored, accountable owner assigned, approval evidence and review dates recorded; monitor obligations and exit rights.</li></ol><p><strong>Central principle:</strong> “We build partnerships to strengthen TIKVARON, never to surrender its independence.” Research, an email, programme invitation or verbal promise is not an agreement.</p></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><h4>Founder approval and authority rules</h4><ul>
      <li>Only the founder may approve a new strategic partnership, commercial sponsorship, accelerator/investor relationship or material supplier agreement on behalf of TIKVARON under this policy.</li><li>Research, introductions, non-binding discovery conversations and draft preparation do not constitute approval to commit.</li><li>No one may sign, accept binding online terms, promise exclusivity, commit spending, share sensitive data or make public claims without explicit founder approval.</li><li>Approval applies only to the exact final document/version, counterparty, scope, price and term reviewed. Material changes require renewed approval.</li><li>Equity, IP transfer, exclusivity, joint venture, guarantees, borrowing, uncapped liability or material data rights require separate explicit approval and independent legal review; they are not pre-approved by this policy.</li><li>Silence, meeting attendance, email discussion, programme admission or receipt of credits is not consent to additional terms.</li>
    </ul><div class="partner-note partner-danger"><strong>Automatic stop:</strong> If a counterparty requires TIKVARON to surrender ownership or control as a condition of basic support, do not accept. Pause, document the clause and return it to the founder for a decision.</div></div>
    <div class="partner-panel"><div class="ops-section-head"><div><h4>Central partnership register</h4><p>Record proposed, due-diligence, approved, active, rejected and terminated relationships. Seed entries include verified outreach already sent and researched prospects not yet contacted; none is represented as a confirmed partnership.</p></div><div class="ops-head-actions"><button class="btn small" id="partnerExportCsv" type="button">Export register CSV</button><button class="btn small" id="partnerBackupBtn" type="button">Backup register JSON</button><button class="btn small" id="partnerRestoreBtn" type="button">Restore backup</button><input id="partnerRestoreFile" class="sr-only" type="file" accept="application/json,.json"></div></div>
      <form id="partnerForm" class="partner-form">
        <label>Organisation / counterparty<input id="partnerName" maxlength="120" required placeholder="Organisation name"></label>
        <label>Relationship type<select id="partnerType"><option>Commercial sponsor</option><option>Technology partner</option><option>Agricultural knowledge partner</option><option>Distribution partner</option><option>Accelerator / investor</option><option>Research / ecosystem partner</option><option>Supplier / service provider</option><option>Other</option></select></label>
        <label>Status<select id="partnerStatus"><option>Proposed — not contacted</option><option>Inquiry sent — awaiting response</option><option>Due diligence</option><option>Negotiation</option><option>Approved — not yet active</option><option>Active</option><option>On hold</option><option>Rejected</option><option>Terminated</option></select></label>
        <label>Risk level<select id="partnerRisk"><option>Unassessed</option><option>Low</option><option>Medium</option><option>High</option><option>Critical</option></select></label>
        <label>Risk likelihood<select id="partnerRiskLikelihood"><option value="">Not assessed</option><option>Rare</option><option>Unlikely</option><option>Possible</option><option>Likely</option><option>Almost certain</option></select></label>
        <label>Risk impact<select id="partnerRiskImpact"><option value="">Not assessed</option><option>Insignificant</option><option>Minor</option><option>Moderate</option><option>Major</option><option>Severe</option></select></label>
        <label>Risk owner<input id="partnerRiskOwner" maxlength="100" placeholder="Accountable reviewer"></label>
        <label>Next risk review date<input id="partnerRiskReviewDate" type="date"></label>
        <label class="wide">Risk mitigation / required control<textarea id="partnerRiskMitigation" maxlength="700" placeholder="Mitigation, evidence required, conditions to clear the risk"></textarea></label>
        <label>Country / jurisdiction<input id="partnerCountry" maxlength="100" placeholder="Country where counterparty is based"></label>
        <label>Official website<input id="partnerWebsite" maxlength="250" placeholder="https://..."></label>
        <label>Official contact email<input id="partnerContactEmail" maxlength="180" placeholder="Public business contact used"></label>
        <label>Outreach message reference(s)<input id="partnerMessageRef" maxlength="300" placeholder="Gmail thread/message ID(s), or not contacted"></label>
        <label>Last contact date<input id="partnerLastContact" type="date"></label>
        <label class="wide">Value offered to TIKVARON<textarea id="partnerValue" maxlength="700" placeholder="Funding, technical capacity, farmer access, expertise, credits, introductions…"></textarea></label>
        <label class="wide">What the counterparty requests from TIKVARON<textarea id="partnerAsk" maxlength="700" placeholder="Fees, deliverables, data, IP licence, publicity, exclusivity, equity, commitments…"></textarea></label>
        <label class="wide">Ownership / IP / exclusivity / data terms<textarea id="partnerTerms" maxlength="900" placeholder="Summarise exact proposed terms or write 'Not yet supplied'."></textarea></label>
        <label>Evidence / contact / source<input id="partnerEvidence" maxlength="300" placeholder="Email date, official page, named contact…"></label>
        <label>Next action / review date<input id="partnerNext" maxlength="300" placeholder="Await reply; review on date…"></label>
        <label class="wide">Due-diligence notes<textarea id="partnerNotes" maxlength="900" placeholder="Evidence, unresolved questions, score and decision rationale…"></textarea></label>
        <label>Evaluation score (0–35)<input id="partnerScore" type="number" min="0" max="35" step="1" placeholder="Score only with evidence"></label>
        <label>Founder approval evidence<input id="partnerApprovalEvidence" maxlength="400" placeholder="Approval date, decision record, exact version"></label>
        <label class="wide">Legal review evidence<input id="partnerLegalEvidence" maxlength="400" placeholder="Reviewer / firm, date, review scope and outcome"></label>
        <label class="wide">Signed agreement reference<input id="partnerAgreementRef" maxlength="400" placeholder="Library path / document ID / signed date (never store passwords or secrets)"></label>
        <div class="partner-checks"><label><input type="checkbox" id="partnerFounderApproved"> Founder explicitly approved exact terms</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="partnerLegalReviewed"> Legal review completed</label><label><input type="checkbox" id="partnerSigned"> Final agreement signed</label></div>
        <div class="wide"><button class="btn primary" type="submit">Add partnership record</button> <span class="filter-summary">Approved status requires documented founder approval and legal review. Active status additionally requires a signed-agreement reference.</span></div>
      </form>
      <div class="partner-actions"><input id="partnerFilter" class="filter" placeholder="Filter organisation or terms" aria-label="Filter partnership register"><select id="partnerStatusFilter" class="filter"><option value="">All statuses</option><option>Proposed — not contacted</option><option>Inquiry sent — awaiting response</option><option>Due diligence</option><option>Negotiation</option><option>Approved — not yet active</option><option>Active</option><option>On hold</option><option>Rejected</option><option>Terminated</option></select></div>
      <div class="partner-note"><strong>Register verification snapshot · 16 November 2026:</strong> 15 outbound email messages verified in the Sent mailbox across 14 organisation records (QSTP received two distinct routing messages). Every sent record carries its recipient and Gmail thread reference. No signed partnership, paid pilot, investment, grant or active commercial relationship is verified. Four additional prospects are research-only; two records are on hold.</div>
      <div id="partnerStats" class="ops-kpis" aria-live="polite"></div>
      <div id="partnerRegister" class="partner-table-wrap"></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="operationsView" hidden aria-label="TIKVARON operating cockpit">
    <div class="ops-banner">
      <div><div class="eyebrow">Company stage / execution system</div><h3>TIKVARON Operating Cockpit</h3><p>Current operating posture: pre-revenue, no discretionary spend without founder approval, and FarmVoice commercial validation before full product development. This cockpit makes the minimum viable business systems active while keeping later-stage enterprise capabilities in the portfolio.</p></div>
      <div class="ops-lock"><strong>BUILD GATE: CLOSED</strong><span>FarmVoice full build stays paused until a paid sponsor, written scope, budget/procurement route and agronomy governance are evidenced.</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-kpis">
      <div class="ops-kpi"><b id="opsOpenCount">0</b><span>Open actions</span></div>
      <div class="ops-kpi"><b id="opsBlockedCount">0</b><span>Blocked / waiting</span></div>
      <div class="ops-kpi"><b id="opsDoneCount">0</b><span>Completed actions</span></div>
      <div class="ops-kpi"><b id="opsCostReady">0/6</b><span>Pilot cost inputs</span></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Minimum viable business system</div><h3>Seven systems to run now</h3><p>Keep the first operating stack lightweight. Status reflects evidence currently available, not software purchase or installation.</p></div></div>
      <div class="starter-grid" id="starterGrid"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Execution register</div><h3>Current operating actions</h3><p>Assign owners, dates and status. Updates are saved in this browser and can be exported or backed up.</p></div><div class="ops-head-actions"><button class="btn small" id="opsExportCsv" type="button">Export actions CSV</button><button class="btn small" id="opsBackupBtn" type="button">Backup operating data</button></div></div>
      <form id="addActionForm" class="add-action-form">
        <input id="newActionTitle" maxlength="140" placeholder="Add a concrete action…" aria-label="New action title" required>
        <select id="newActionWorkstream" aria-label="New action workstream"><option>Commercial validation</option><option>Finance & unit economics</option><option>Product & engineering</option><option>Legal & privacy</option><option>Security</option><option>Agronomy governance</option><option>Business operations</option></select>
        <input id="newActionOwner" maxlength="80" placeholder="Owner / role" aria-label="New action owner">
        <input id="newActionDue" type="date" aria-label="Due date">
        <button class="btn primary" type="submit">Add action</button>
      </form>
      <div id="opsTaskList" class="ops-task-list"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">FarmVoice paid-pilot unit economics</div><h3>Cost-to-serve calculator</h3><p>Enter supplier quotes and realistic delivery costs. No rates are prefilled or invented. This is an editable model, not a quote or accounting record.</p></div></div>
      <div class="calc-grid">
        <div class="calc-inputs">
          <label>Farmers in pilot<input type="number" id="calcFarmers" min="1" step="1" value="100"></label>
          <label>Pilot duration (weeks)<input type="number" id="calcWeeks" min="1" step="1" value="12"></label>
          <label>One-time setup + content cost (KES)<input type="number" id="calcSetup" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter actual quote"></label>
          <label>AI + voice cost per farmer / month (KES)<input type="number" id="calcAiUnit" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter provider-based estimate"></label>
          <label>Messaging / WhatsApp cost per farmer / month (KES)<input type="number" id="calcMsgUnit" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter actual tariff"></label>
          <label>Agronomist / escalation cover per month (KES)<input type="number" id="calcAgroMonthly" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter agreed cost"></label>
          <label>Support / coordinator per month (KES)<input type="number" id="calcSupportMonthly" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter actual cost"></label>
          <label>Field travel / training fixed cost (KES)<input type="number" id="calcField" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter estimate or quote"></label>
          <label>Other fixed cost (KES)<input type="number" id="calcOther" min="0" step="0.01" placeholder="Enter amount or 0"></label>
          <label>Contingency (%)<input type="number" id="calcContingency" min="0" max="100" step="0.5" placeholder="Set after risk review"></label>
          <label>Target gross margin (%)<input type="number" id="calcMargin" min="0" max="95" step="1" placeholder="Set pricing target"></label>
        </div>
        <div class="calc-results">
          <div class="calc-readiness" id="calcReadiness">0 of 6 core cost inputs entered · not quote-ready</div>
          <div class="calc-result"><span>Estimated delivery cost</span><strong id="calcTotal">—</strong></div>
          <div class="calc-result"><span>Minimum sponsor fee at target margin</span><strong id="calcFee">—</strong></div>
          <div class="calc-result"><span>Cost per farmer</span><strong id="calcPerFarmer">—</strong></div>
          <div class="calc-result"><span>Fee per farmer</span><strong id="calcFeePerFarmer">—</strong></div>
          <p id="calcWarning">Enter the six core cost inputs using actual supplier, agronomist and delivery estimates. A fee should not be proposed until inputs and scope are validated.</p>
          <button class="btn small" type="button" id="calcReset">Clear cost inputs</button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">Stage-gated activation</div><h3>Build now / activate later</h3><p>The full catalogue is a capability map, not a shopping list. Do not procure enterprise tooling before a real business need and budget trigger exists.</p></div></div>
      <div class="stage-roadmap">
        <article><h4>Pre-revenue · now</h4><ul><li>CRM and sponsor pipeline — active locally</li><li>Security hygiene and secrets discipline — validate and document</li><li>Legal/privacy basics — prepare before farmer data or pilot agreement</li><li>AI cost-to-serve model — calculator is ready; populate real costs</li><li>Weekly review and decision log — use this cockpit</li><li>Paid-pilot concept note and sponsor qualification — active work</li></ul></article>
        <article><h4>First revenue · after signed pilot</h4><ul><li>Invoicing and accounts receivable</li><li>Accounting system selected for actual jurisdiction and tax needs</li><li>Customer support inbox and pilot knowledge base</li><li>Live product usage, reliability and margin telemetry</li><li>Vendor/procurement and contract records</li></ul></article>
        <article><h4>$1M ARR · when justified</h4><ul><li>Formal SOC 2 / ISO programme, customer success tooling</li><li>FinOps automation and pricing operations</li><li>Dedicated HR, reporting and compliance processes</li><li>Advanced analytics and portfolio governance</li></ul></article>
        <article><h4>$10M ARR / enterprise · trigger-led</h4><ul><li>Formal treasury, tax and multi-entity controls</li><li>Enterprise risk, audit and insurance programmes</li><li>Multi-region and sector-specific compliance</li><li>Formal board, procurement and resilience operations</li></ul></article>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">AI operator protocol</div><h3>How ChatGPT should run TIKVARON operations</h3><p>This is the working instruction set for business tasks in our conversations; it does not change ChatGPT's underlying model or automatically connect every SaaS tool.</p></div></div>
      <div class="governance-grid">
        <div><strong>Commercial priority</strong><p>Qualify and secure a paid FarmVoice pilot sponsor before expanding product development.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Approval gates</strong><p>Prepare and recommend freely; obtain explicit approval before external messages, spending, agreements, deployments or production changes.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Evidence discipline</strong><p>Label verified facts, estimates and assumptions separately. Never claim a task, integration or payment is complete without confirmation.</p></div>
        <div><strong>One operating record</strong><p>Keep decisions, owners, actions, maturity, risks and costs in the register. Export backups because this file stores data locally.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div class="ops-section">
      <div class="ops-section-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">System-of-systems governance</div><h3>How to manage the 100-category portfolio</h3><p>Use the Manage control on any inventory row to set its operating decision and review controls.</p></div></div>
      <div class="governance-grid">
        <div><strong>Build / Buy / Defer / Kill</strong><p>Decide based on current stage, actual pain, risk, cost and strategic advantage—not completeness of the catalogue.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Cost of ownership</strong><p>Record monthly KES cost, implementation burden and dependencies before approving a purchase.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Evidence-based maturity</strong><p>Not Started → Ad hoc → Defined → Managed → Optimized. Unrated means no assessment has been made.</p></div>
        <div><strong>Review rhythm</strong><p>Weekly execution review, monthly business review and quarterly portfolio review. Record a date and named owner for critical systems.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
  <footer class="footer"><span><strong>Where Hope Sings.</strong> Hard problems. Real hope.</span><span>Single-file local tool · No external libraries · Browser-local storage only (not cloud synced) · If storage is blocked, export JSON backups before closing</span></footer>
</main>

<div class="system-modal" id="systemModal" hidden role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-labelledby="systemModalTitle">
  <div class="system-modal-panel">
    <div class="modal-head"><div><div class="eyebrow">System operating record</div><h3 id="systemModalTitle">Manage system</h3><p id="systemModalMeta"></p></div><button class="btn small" type="button" id="systemModalClose">Close</button></div>
    <form id="systemModalForm" class="system-modal-grid">
      <input type="hidden" id="manageSystemId">
      <label>Operating decision<select id="manageDecision"><option>Unassessed</option><option>Build</option><option>Buy</option><option>Defer</option><option>Kill</option></select></label>
      <label>Operating status<select id="manageStatus"><option>Not started</option><option>Research</option><option>Planned</option><option>In progress</option><option>Operating</option><option>Blocked</option><option>Retired</option></select></label>
      <label>Estimated monthly cost (KES)<input type="number" min="0" step="0.01" id="manageCost" placeholder="Unknown / not yet costed"></label>
      <label>Review cadence<select id="manageCadence"><option value="">Not set</option><option>Weekly</option><option>Monthly</option><option>Quarterly</option><option>Annually</option><option>Event-driven</option></select></label>
      <label>Next review date<input type="date" id="manageReviewDate"></label>
      <label>Dependencies<input id="manageDependencies" maxlength="240" placeholder="Systems or people required first"></label>
      <label class="span-2">Build / activation trigger<textarea id="manageTrigger" maxlength="600" rows="2" placeholder="What measurable event makes this necessary?"></textarea></label>
      <label class="span-2">Evidence / operating notes<textarea id="manageNotes" maxlength="1200" rows="3" placeholder="Record evidence, costs, approvals and decisions. Do not store secrets."></textarea></label>
      <div class="modal-actions"><button class="btn ghost" type="button" id="systemModalCancel">Cancel</button><button class="btn primary" type="submit">Save system record</button></div>
    </form>
  </div>
</div>

<div class="toast" id="toast" role="status"></div>
<script>
'use strict';

// Resilient storage: localStorage can be blocked in private, embedded or file contexts.
// The app remains usable in memory and clearly warns the user to export a backup.
const safeStorage = (() => {
  const memory = new Map();
  let persistent = true;
  return {
    get persistent() { return persistent; },
    getItem(key) {
      try {
        const value = window.localStorage.getItem(key);
        if (value !== null) memory.set(key, value);
        return value !== null ? value : (memory.has(key) ? memory.get(key) : null);
      } catch (err) {
        persistent = false;
        return memory.has(key) ? memory.get(key) : null;
      }
    },
    setItem(key, value) {
      const text = String(value);
      memory.set(key, text);
      try { window.localStorage.setItem(key, text); }
      catch (err) { persistent = false; }
    },
    removeItem(key) {
      memory.delete(key);
      try { window.localStorage.removeItem(key); }
      catch (err) { persistent = false; }
    }
  };
})();
